er": "JPM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 1.1977, "filing_name": "JPMorgan Chase & Co 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026008131/jpm-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 4, "dropped_candidates": 134, "token_estimate": 30891, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "JPMorgan Chase reported net interest income of $95,443 million for fiscal 2025 (year ended December 31, 2025) in its consolidated statements of income [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0538]. This compares with $92,583 million for fiscal 2024 [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0538], which is a 3.1% increase computed from the two reported values. On a managed basis, net interest income was $95,868 million, after fully taxable-equivalent adjustments of $425 million [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0074]. Excluding Markets, net interest income was $92,591 million [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0074].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "JPM", "company": "JPMorgan Chase & Co", "findings": [{"point": "Reported net interest income for fiscal 2025 (ended December 31, 2025) was $95,443 million, versus $92,583 million for fiscal 2024.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0538"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Managed-basis net interest income was $95,868 million, and net interest income excluding Markets was $92,591 million, for fiscal 2025.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0074"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The firm attributes the increase to higher Markets net interest income, higher Card Services revolving balances, higher wholesale deposit balances and investment securities activity, largely offset by deposit margin compression and lower rates.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0020"], "unverified": false}]}], "compari